# M6 4c (slice 347; Codex CODEX-OPUS-347-4C-INIT-REPLY-20261110T071350Z-01 A, CODEX-OPUS-347-4C-ROUTE-REPLY item 1): the
# formal gets the Structure written in the code; its computed field `y: int: k + 5` belongs to that written body and
# does not run when a reference to it is given, so the Structure has no int place y yet and the formal p, whose model
# reads p\y as an int, refuses it at admission when the call is reached (4) -- neither a hidden run (62) nor an invented
# 0. `before` is computed, `after` never.
Point:
    int: y 0
end: Point
fn: take (Point: p; int: q 2) int
    return: p\y * 10 + q
end: take
int: k 1
int: before 1
int: r take(p: y: int: k + 5)
int: after before + 1
